Add the 3D Hardware Engineer die as a spatial storytelling layer

The die section now renders an original abstract SoC floorplan in WebGL:
dark package, I/O perimeter, raised functional regions, an interconnect
spine with travelling signals, and an instanced memory array on CURRENT.

Deliberate choices:
- No GSAP. useSectionProgress already is a deterministic, reversible
  scroll state machine; ScrollTrigger would duplicate it.
- Nothing readable is drawn into WebGL. Region names are DOM overlays
  anchored to geometry; all copy stays in the annotation column.
- The camera is moved by scroll state only, damped, never orbiting.
  Pointer parallax is capped at a fraction of a unit.
- Semantic zoom leans toward a region rather than diving at it, so the
  floorplan stays readable and the reader keeps their bearings.
- The existing SVG die is the fallback for phones, reduced motion and
  any machine without a usable WebGL context. It is fully interactive,
  so no engineering information depends on WebGL.
- The scene is a lazy chunk: main bundle grew 1.3 kB gzip; the 239 kB
  three chunk is never fetched on the fallback paths. Frame loop stops
  when the section is off screen; DPR capped at 1.75.

